{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966804,"nonce":"UAqiJ+DG5RWJlb/Xuz6ZnkyNFVE=","title":"cn.Textarea inflated its ancestor 519-\u003e929 on frame 2: it baked its MEASURED width into the","message":"**Symptom.** In `cn_playground`, a large vertical gap sat between\n`FormWidgets` and `FeedbackWidgets` on launch, then closed: the sections below\nvisibly shifted a frame later. Removing `cn.Textarea` removed it. Any FSM\nbutton also cleared it, which wrongly implicated rebuilds.\n\n**Root cause (fixed, 9691a4fe).** Two things compounding.\n\n1. `TextArea::layout_bounds_callback` writes the measured bounds into\n   `cfg.width`, then `refresh_stateful`. The rebuilt content wrapper emitted\n   that value as a FIXED style width (`div().w(config.effective_width())`).\n   So frame 1 built at the 300px default and frame 2 at the measured width.\n2. The measured width equals the parent's available width by construction,\n   and a child EXACTLY filling its parent tips taffy into sizing the ancestor\n   by min-content. The section went 519 -\u003e 929, which is its min-content\n   height (every `flex_wrap: wrap` row collapses to one item per line).\n\nA width sweep on the textarea's five nodes pins the edge precisely:\n\n    Auto / Percent(1.0) / 600 / 671  -\u003e tops [24, 559, 808]   correct\n    672 (== available width)         -\u003e tops [24, 969, 1219]  the bug\n\n**Fix.** `TextAreaConfig::width_is_explicit`, set only by `w`/`cols`/`size`/\n`text_size`. The wrapper emits a style width only when that flag is set;\notherwise it stays auto-width and is stretched by its parent. `cfg.width` is\nstill updated by the callback because text wrapping needs it. `TextInput`\nalready worked this way (`w_full()` / auto plus `min_w(0)`, `computed_width`\nfor metrics only) -- the textarea was the odd one out.\n\n**General hazard worth remembering:** never emit a measured size back as a\nfixed style size. It lands on the exact available width every time, which is\ntaffy's pathological equality case, and it turns a fluid box rigid so every\nancestor's intrinsic sizing changes on the second frame.\n\n**Diagnosis technique that finally worked** (`crates/blinc_cn_dsl/tests/\npg_settle.rs`, now passing and un-ignored): snapshot EVERY node across both\nframes -- depth, height, y, content_size, child count, and the full taffy\nStyle -- then diff. Height and child diffs said \"nothing changed\"; the STYLE\ndiff immediately named the five textarea nodes whose width went 300 -\u003e 672.\nAlso added `LayoutTree::taffy_child_count` to prove no orphaned taffy children\n(`children()` silently drops any child missing from `reverse_map`).\n\n**Dead ends, each measured:** content_size propagation (content_h stayed 519\nin both frames); collapsing-animation style overrides (zero registered); a\nstale taffy cache (a 3rd and 4th `compute_layout` stayed at 929); `flex_shrink`\nand `min_size` clamping (shrink=0 plus min-height=0 still gave 929); text\nmeasurement (no wrapped measurement returns a tall result); `layout_style`\nforwarding (a genuine bug, `90fe7dcd`, but not this one).\n\n**Why headless work kept saying \"correct\":** `compute_layout` reads the built\nnode. The diff and refresh paths read the BUILDER. A defect that lives on the\nsecond frame needs a two-frame harness: build, `process_pending_subtree_\nrebuilds()`, re-measure.\n\nRelated: `auto_create_css_scroll_physics` skips nodes that already own physics,\nand the playground creates ZERO CSS physics, so nothing inside the textarea\ngets a second scroller. That earlier suspicion is cleared.\n\nSee gotcha button stale size on label change,\ngotcha element builder trait forwarding,\ngotcha text min content inflation.","files":null}]}